From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:56:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] A mod's Remix Logic option layer: only its own config file,
 only rendering options

The GMod loader deploys the Remix mods of any subscribed Workshop item as content. An RtxOptionLayerAction node in
such a mod's graph acquired an option layer, above rtx.conf, from any config file it named (a UNC path made Windows
offer the player's login to another host), the file could set every runtime option (the folder NRC loads its CUDA
DLLs from, the welcome message the splash formatted as printf, captures, keys), and a hash list that failed to parse
(std::stoull) threw out of the graph and ended the game.

- rtx_mod_layer_policy.h (new, self-contained): the path rules (relative as authored, inside the mod's folder once
  resolved; at the option manager, a file in a mod's folder below rtx-remix/mods, no "." or "..", no share other
  than the game's, no stream, no device), the options a mod's layer may set (the sky, the weather, fog and volumetric
  light, exposure, tone mapping, bloom and post effects, and eight single look options; never text, lists, keys or
  integer vectors, never an integer without a declared range of at most 1024 values, never a debugging option, a name
  ending as a file, folder, message or key, the player's own settings or runtime state) and a parse that reports
  instead of throwing.
- The graph's parser: in a mod's stage, an asset path that names a drive, a root, a share or a scheme is refused
  before the resolver looks for it, and what it resolves to must lie in the mod's folder; a string-typed asset path
  resolves as a token does. In-memory stages keep upstream's resolution.
- RtxOptionManager::acquireModLayer: the graph's layers, with the path checked against the mods folder; the layer is
  marked a mod's layer, which applies only the allowed options (the others count as rejected keys, kept on save, and
  are logged once) and creates no dynamic options. A mod's graph and code never share a layer.
- Any layer, and readOption (the Remix API's SetConfigVariable): a value that fails to parse is refused and leaves
  the value as it was; SetConfigVariable returns INVALID_ARGUMENTS for it. RtxOptionLayerAction catches what
  acquiring a layer could still throw.

tests/rtx/unit/test_mod_layer_policy.cpp covers the policy alone (also compiled by the project's gate);
test_mod_option_layer.cpp drives a mod's layer through the real option manager (refused paths, a file in a mod's
folder, reload, a code layer and readOption with a hash list that fails to parse).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
